Recommends: lsscsi, mt-st, mtx
Description: virtual tape library for Linux
 mhvtl emulates a SCSI medium changer and SCSI tape drives entirely in
 software. It consists of a pseudo HBA kernel module and a pair of
 user-space daemons, vtllibrary and vtltape, which act as the SCSI
 targets. Tape media is stored as regular files on disk.
 .
 It is used to test and develop backup and archival software without
 physical tape hardware. It emulates LTO, DLT and AIT tape drives, and
 tape libraries from vendors such as IBM, HP, Quantum and Spectra Logic.
 .
 This package provides the user-space daemons, command line tools and
 systemd units. The kernel module is supplied by mhvtl-dkms.

Package: mhvtl-dkms
Section: kernel
Architecture: all
Depends:
 dkms,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers
Description: virtual tape library for Linux - kernel module source
 mhvtl emulates a SCSI medium changer and SCSI tape drives entirely in
 software, for testing backup and archival applications without physical
 tape hardware.
 .
 This package provides the source of the mhvtl pseudo HBA kernel module.
 DKMS builds it for the running kernel on installation and rebuilds it
 whenever a new kernel is installed. Kernel headers matching the running
 kernel must be present for the build to succeed.
